From 07bb78ba31115133a03bfb8a4cd04cffe8b04327 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:55:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] EDITION ONLY: show the 3D area of a video in a surface of
 its own, as stereo content

Sparky Stereo OS (not for Qt's own tree): where the Wayland compositor takes
stereo content (kde_stereo_content_manager_v1, declared with libstereo-declare),
VideoOutput shows a stereoscopic 3D video in a Wayland subsurface of its
own under the window's surface, declared as full side by side stereo content,
left eye first, and the window's own surface keeps what a player draws over
the video (the controls, the same in both eyes): the separation of a window's 2D
part from its 3D area. A player that binds stereoView, stereoInput and
stereoSwapEyes to its menu says nothing else.

 - The views are taken apart from the frame's floating point image on the GPU
   (Float32 for 16 bit video), restored to full size with the filter stereoScaling
   names, packed side by side, and written into a shared memory buffer of the
   depth stereoSurface names, as deep as the compositor offers: 8 bits
   (XRGB8888), 10 (XRGB2101010), 16 (XBGR16161616) or half float.
 - The item itself is a transparent hole: a node that writes (0, 0, 0, 0)
   over what is drawn behind it, so the window's background, a page's, a black
   rectangle, need no change; what is drawn over it stays. The window needs an
   alpha buffer from its creation, which VideoOutput asks for when the compositor
   takes stereo content.
 - The colour description of the video goes to the compositor with
   wp_color_management_v1 where it has it: BT.2020 primaries, the PQ, HLG or
   linear transfer function, and the mastering display's peak luminance. SDR
   video in BT.709 is not described (the compositor's default), so that it
   looks as it does without the layer.
 - A frame sequence is paired in order and shown as two frames of the pair.
 - Everything is off without the compositor, a window that has no alpha buffer, a
   rotated or mirrored video, or QT_NO_STEREO_LAYER at build time: then one view
   is shown in the scene graph, as the previous change does.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
